+**Orphaned turn leases.** A turn holds its session's lease while it runs and
+releases it when it ends. If that release cannot be written (the state.db write
+lock was held past the write patience), the lease stays until it expires, up to
+300 seconds after the turn, and a model pick on the now idle chat is deferred
+to the next turn, while a reset or compress is refused as busy. Set
+`sessions.reclaim_orphaned_turn_leases: true` so the gateway reclaims a lease it
+wrote itself as soon as no turn of the same process holds it:
+
+```yaml
+sessions:
+  reclaim_orphaned_turn_leases: true
+```
+
+A lease written by another process is still kept until it expires or that
+process is gone.
+
 ### Oversized-Transcript Guards
 
 Two limits stop a runaway transcript from being loaded into memory all at once
